WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.127
There is no single best vector database for every RAG project.

00:00:04.127 --> 00:00:12.802
For a notebook or small class project, NumPy, FAISS, or Chroma may be the best choice because they

00:00:12.802 --> 00:00:13.482
are simple and transparent.

00:00:13.482 --> 00:00:19.917
For a small application that needs persistence and filtering, Chroma or Qdrant may be practical.

00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:28.122
If the organization already depends heavily on PostgreSQL, pgvector may reduce architectural complexity.

00:00:28.122 --> 00:00:29.042
[tts-break]

00:00:29.042 --> 00:00:36.472
For managed cloud deployment, teams may evaluate services such as Pinecone or hosted versions of Qdrant,

00:00:36.472 --> 00:00:38.492
Weaviate, or Zilliz.

00:00:38.492 --> 00:00:45.187
The decision should consider document volume, update frequency, metadata filtering, latency, security, cost,

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:48.617
backup requirements, and team skills.

00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:53.602
Do not choose a database only because it appears frequently in tutorials.

00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:59.667
The storage layer should support the needs of the application and the organization.
